    "case_summary": "A 32-year-old woman presented with a 2-week history of back and loin pain, heaviness in her thighs, intermittent fever, and rigors. Medical history included trigeminal neuralgia and pervasive anxiety, for which she had recently started quetiapine.\n\nTemperature was 39°C. No other abnormal physical findings were noted.\n\n- Laboratory Tests:    * Initial blood count and biochemical profile normal except raised C-reactive protein (118 mg/L, normal <4 mg/L)    * Urine and blood cultures were sterile    * Creatine Kinase elevated (30.51 μkat/L, normal 0.42–3.34 μkat/L)    * Hemoglobin decreased to 93 g/L from 126 g/L    * Neutropenia (0.9 × 10⁹/L; normal 2.0–7.5 × 10⁹/L)    * Thrombocytopenia (110 × 10⁹/L; normal 150–400 × 10⁹/L)    * Serum ferritin markedly elevated (34,844 pmol/L; normal 29–337 pmol/L)    * Elevated LDH (10.55 μkat/L; normal 2.0–4.1 μkat/L)    * Anti-myositis antibodies negative    * Autoantibody screens negative    * Normal serum complement (C3/C4)- Imaging Studies:    * CT of renal tract: normal    * Chest radiograph: normal    * Echocardiogram: normal    * PET-CT Image Title: 18F-FDG PET-CT of Axial Skeleton    * PET-CT Description: Diffusely increased, non-homogeneous FDG uptake in the axial skeleton    * MRI Image Title: Spine MRI    * MRI Description: Marrow signal abnormalities with patchy muscle and fascial edema within iliopsoas and obturator externus muscles bilaterally- Pathological Studies:    * Muscle Biopsy: Non-specific small group atrophy    * Initial Bone Marrow Biopsy: Cellular marrow with fibrotic changes    * Third Bone Marrow Biopsy: Near-total effacement of marrow by necrotic, high-grade tumor    * Immunohistochemistry: Positive for CD2, cytoplasmic CD3, CD30, perforin, TIA-1; Negative for CD4, CD5, CD7, CD8, TCR-gamma, ALK-1    * Karyotype: −43–45,XX,–5,–10,–15,add(15)(p10),–22,+mar1,+mar2,+mar3[cp8]/46,XX[18]",
